flf2a$ 3 3 25 -1 35 0 0 2538

PHM's Large Type font for FIGlet
by Philippe Majerus (www.phm.lu)

This font uses Unicode 16 Large Type Pieces (U+1CE1A to U+1CE50) and
Quadrants (including the centered variants) to build a smooth set of
characters using three rows. It also uses Sextants and Octants for some
non-alphabetical characters such as Braille, outlined letters and
7-segment digits.
It requires the terminal to support those characters to display properly.

Included characters:
• Latin
   • Latin-1 (Basic Latin and Latin-1 Supplement blocks)
   • Latin Extended-A
   • Latin Extended-B
   • Latin Extended Additional
   • Superscripts, subscripts, and small capitals
   • Number Forms
• Greek
• Cyrillic
• Japanese half-width katakana (JIS X 0201)
• Some mathematical operators and symbols
• Braille patterns
• Pseudo-pixels mosaics (Quadrants, Sextants, Octants, Separated Quadrants, Separated Sextants)
• Miscellaneous (extra symbols, outlined capital letters and numbers, segmented digits, …)
Remember to use "figlet -C utf8" to access Unicode characters.
This font does not support "smushing" (-S) and large characters will get
mangled, and "kerning" (-k) has no effect.

Date: January 15 to April 28, 2024 ; Latin Extended-B + Additional, Braille: November 10 - 12,
2024, Misc. March 20, 2025 to August 3, 2025, Trigrams, Double-Struck, and fixes January 2026,
Large Type Pieces August 2026.


